<title>USA: Rivlin says pleased by U.S. budget agreement.</title>
<headline>Rivlin says pleased by U.S. budget agreement.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Reserve Vice Chair Alice Rivlin on Tuesday welcomed the budget agreement between the White House and Republican leaders and said she believed it would lead to a balanced federal budget.</p>
<p>&quot;I think it's good that they have got (an agreement),&quot; Rivlin said on her way into the House Banking Committee.</p>
<p>She also said she was &quot;very gratified&quot; that the budget deficit was falling as fast as it is.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
